60,3,1,talk,George,,Option C creates a favour-asking trap. Option B is rigid but predictable. I lean towards B to protect our peace.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option B eliminates the bookkeeping entirely. Fixed days, fixed cost. No dial photos, no squaring receipts. It is the only way to stop the administrative bleed.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option B guarantees my day, but does it guarantee the car is clean and fueled? I need a physical check before I drive.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option B hides the variable costs. If I drive far, I subsidize the others. I need the split to reflect actual usage, not just days.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option B feels simple and kind. I worry about the car being ready, but I like that everyone has their own day.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,George,,"@Victoria, the physical check is essential. We must agree on a handover standard to prevent the friction you described.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, a fixed handover standard is manageable. If the car is not ready, the next person simply does not use it. No arguments, just consequences.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, consequences are not comfort. I need a guarantee that the car is clean and fueled before my specific weekly trip.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Victoria, a guarantee is just a rule. I need the numbers to show who is actually paying for the distance, not just the day.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I agree. Maybe we can just check the car together before leaving? It feels safer that way.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,George,,"@Minato, checking together is a favour. It invites the very friction we are trying to avoid. We need a standard, not a meeting.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Minato, checking together is a meeting. I need a standard that requires no one to ask. Option B is the only one that ends the negotiation.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, a standard is good, but it does not fix the empty tank. I need the car to be physically ready, not just available.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Toshio, a standard is not a ledger. Option B ignores the 280,000 yen baseline. I need the split to reflect actual distance, not just days.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Misaki, I understand the worry about the numbers. But I think Option B is the kindest. It gives everyone a safe, quiet day without asking.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,George,,I am voting for B. Predictability protects the peace.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I am voting for B. It ends the bookkeeping and the negotiation.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I am voting for B. Predictability is essential, but I need a strict handover standard to ensure the car is physically ready for my trip.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I am voting for A. It is the only option that accounts for actual distance, ensuring no one quietly subsidizes the others.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,I am voting for B. It feels the most peaceful and fair for everyone.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
